* @title Reclaim a built-in name with UNLOAD
* @expect >>>
* SIZE OF CAT IS 3
* reused as a variable
* <<<
* UNLOAD removes a function definition, so the name reverts to an ordinary
* variable. After UNLOAD('SIZE'), the built-in SIZE function is gone and SIZE
* becomes a plain variable we can assign to.
        OUTPUT = 'SIZE OF CAT IS ' SIZE('CAT')
        UNLOAD('SIZE')
        SIZE = 'reused as a variable'
        OUTPUT = SIZE
END
